# `yo fix <path> --migrate unsized` rewrites every `dyn(v)` site of a plain
# value by its recorded position: a template literal, an interpolation, a
# bracket or an escaped quote inside a string, and an argument over several
# lines with a comment are rewritten `dyn(Box.new(v))`
# (issues/fixed/2026-11-15-migrate-unsized-lists-one-line-dyn-sites-holding-a-template-literal-or-a-bracket-in-a-string.md).
# An enum variant named `Dyn` is left alone
# (issues/fixed/2026-11-15-migrate-unsized-rewrites-an-enum-variant-named-dyn.md),
# and so is a `dyn` site inside a `comptime_expect_error` argument. The second
# run is a no-op and the file still type-checks.
fix . --migrate unsized
fix . --migrate unsized
check main.yo
